      "formula": "f'(3)=lim_(h arrow.r 0)(6+h)=6",
      "text": "As the second input approaches three, the slope approaches six. The limiting secant becomes the tangent line. This instantaneous rate is defined by nearby changes, not by directly substituting zero into the original difference quotient.",
