      "formula": "f(x)=abs(x): quad f'(0) \"does not exist\"",
      "text": "A derivative does not always exist. At the corner of absolute x, left-hand slopes approach negative one while right-hand slopes approach positive one. The function is continuous there, but no single tangent slope fits both approaches.",
